lopedia/campania">Campania</a> weakens.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">396 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> destroys Veii after a ten-year siege; from the same year the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a> invade the Po Valley.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">358 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Tarquinia and Caere ally against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">310 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a> are defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> at Lake Vadimone.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">264 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Volsinii, seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fanum-voltumnae">Fanum Voltumnae</a>, is defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>; the league's independence ends.</span></li></ol>
